#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-AD0450 expect=violation domain=ADLBC
#note "O-3 (Fix #336): was `skipped_index_out_of_filter` pinning `_wildcards: y: {min: 1, max: 9}`. The owner ruled y = 1-99 on EVERY _wildcards entry (ADaMIG v1.1+ §3.1.1 'an integer [1-99, not zero-padded]'), so index TEN is now inside the filter, MCRIT10ML/MCRIT10MN match, and the populated ML with a missing MN fires - the same verdict PMDA-AD0339-invalid_two_digit_index already pinned for its MCRIT-family column at index 10. The filter-as-FILTER pin lives on in the sibling `skipped_index_hundred_filtered`."
#library standard=adamig version=1-3
dataset ADLBC structure=BDS
col STUDYID     type=Char
col USUBJID     type=Char
col PARAMCD     type=Char
col MCRIT10ML   type=Char
col MCRIT10MN   type=Num
---
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 | ALT | PARTIAL |
---
#expectViolationCount 1
